# Orkestra runtime data
**/.orkestra/.trak/
**/.orkestra/.database/
**/.orkestra/.processes.json*
**/.orkestra/records/
**/.orkestra/.snapshots/
**/.orkestra/.setup/
.orkestra/.logs/
**/.orkestra/.worktrees/
.orkestra/.screenshots/
**/.orkestra/.local/
# The one committed overlay in the repository: `test/e2e/library-from-disk.test.ts` points
# the loader at it, so it has to sit at exactly this path and it has to be in git. Once the
# line above gained its `**/` prefix it matched here too — and a directory rule stops git
# descending, so a fixture added under it would silently never be committed. Negating the
# directory itself is what lets git back in; `!…/.local/**` would not.
!test/fixtures/overlay/.orkestra/.local/
**/.orkestra/.cache/

# Scratch from the globally-installed `playwright-cli` dev tool, which writes into cwd
.playwright-cli/

# Where an `experiment` step works. Ignoring this path is the whole mechanism that lets a
# write step throw its code away: `commitWork` stages with `git add -A`, so a probe script
# and whatever it installed never reach the trak's branch, and the step's commit is empty.
# It sits inside the checkout rather than in a temp directory so an experiment can compile
# against this repo's own types and node_modules. Nothing here is kept: the finding goes
# in the artifact, and the directory goes with the worktree at close.
.experiments/

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json

# Env
.env
.env.local
!.env.example
.test-repos/

# Claude Code local settings
.claude/settings.local.json

# atelier design studies. The dated month folders are not part of this repository; each
# person keeps their own. The tool files beside them — `atelier.config.json`, `atelier.ts`,
# `live.tsx`, `CLAUDE.md` — are tracked: `atelier dev` reads the config, and every round
# that mounts the real client imports `live.tsx`.
.atelier/20*
.atelier/.*
#
# derived, regenerated on demand
.atelier/**/.shots/
.atelier/.exports/
.atelier/.cache/
.atelier/.log
# a saved decision is its JSON; the picture beside it is reproducible from the round and
# is larger than every .tsx in the study put together
.atelier/**/saved/*.png
# shipped examples, rewritten by every atelier command
.atelier/**/example-*/
# spot checks — thrown away, not kept
.atelier/proof/

# Playwright's own output. The specs are the artefact; a run's report is not.
client/test-results/
client/playwright-report/

# Prompt transcripts, rewritten by every e2e run and read on the machine that ran them.
# They were committed once, so that a prompt edit showed up as a diff — but nobody ever
# read one that way, and the cost was paid on every surface: one five-line edit to a
# shared template rewrites the same text in 216 files, which buries the real change in
# `git diff`, in review, in the reviewing agent's token bill, and in `git log --stat`
# forever. Run the suite and read the file instead; a run is free.
test/e2e/logs/

